{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"docsStarts":1},{"foundation":2,"assurance":3},"/foundation/docs/","/assurance/docs/getting-started/"],"uses":{}},null,{"type":"data","data":[{"docs":1,"source":44},{"nav":2,"slugs":43,"first":6},[3,7,11,15,19,23,27,31,35,39],{"name":4,"href":5,"slug":6},"Getting started","/assurance/docs/getting-started/","getting-started",{"name":8,"href":9,"slug":10},"Scenarios","/assurance/docs/scenarios/","scenarios",{"name":12,"href":13,"slug":14},"Business context","/assurance/docs/business-context/","business-context",{"name":16,"href":17,"slug":18},"Evidence","/assurance/docs/evidence/","evidence",{"name":20,"href":21,"slug":22},"The CLI","/assurance/docs/cli/","cli",{"name":24,"href":25,"slug":26},"Running in CI","/assurance/docs/ci/","ci",{"name":28,"href":29,"slug":30},"Adapters","/assurance/docs/adapters/","adapters",{"name":32,"href":33,"slug":34},"Analyzers","/assurance/docs/analyzers/","analyzers",{"name":36,"href":37,"slug":38},"Privacy","/assurance/docs/privacy/","privacy",{"name":40,"href":41,"slug":42},"Performance","/assurance/docs/performance/","performance",[6,10,14,18,22,26,30,34,38,42],{"repo":45,"version":46},"https://github.com/AHRConsulting/Ahr.Assurance","0.1.0"],"uses":{"params":["product"]}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"page":2},"getting-started",{"slug":1,"title":3,"html":4,"headings":5,"source":19},"Getting started","\u003Ch2 id=\"install\">Install\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Install \u003Ca href=\"/assurance/docs/cli/\">the CLI\u003C/a>, which builds the report, once per repository:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">dotnet\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> tool\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> install\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> Ahr.Assurance.Cli\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>Add the adapter for the test framework to each test project, and create its config file, so each run keeps a folder of its own. The CLI does both, at its own version:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">dotnet\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> assurance\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> init\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> --framework\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> xunit-v3\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-wrap\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Framework\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Adapter\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Ccode>--framework\u003C/code>\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>xUnit v3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.Xunit.v3\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>xunit-v3\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>xUnit v2\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.Xunit.v2\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>xunit-v2\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>NUnit 3.14, 4 or 5\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.NUnit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>nunit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>MSTest 4\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.MSTest\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>mstest\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>MSTest 3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.MSTest.v3\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>mstest-v3\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>TUnit\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.TUnit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>tunit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Add-on:\u003C/strong> browser tests with Playwright, under any framework\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance.Playwright\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>playwright\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>Not sure which one? \u003Ccode>dotnet assurance init\u003C/code> on its own creates the config file, adds no package, and prints the command for the framework the project uses. Run it in a solution's folder to set up each test project. Or add the adapter with NuGet, then run \u003Ccode>dotnet assurance init\u003C/code>:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">dotnet\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> add\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> package\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> Ahr.Assurance.Xunit.v3\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> --version\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-number)\"> 0.1.0\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The adapter brings \u003Ccode>Ahr.Assurance\u003C/code> and its analyzers. It needs .NET 10 or later.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Browser tests?\u003C/strong> Add Playwright too. It works under any adapter, and puts a screenshot of the page at each step into the report:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">dotnet\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> assurance\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> init\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> --framework\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> xunit-v3,playwright\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>Write Playwright as you always do, with \u003Ccode>page.GotoAsync\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>ClickAsync\u003C/code> and your own assertions, inside the steps. The only new line is \u003Ccode>AssurancePlaywright.Capture(page)\u003C/code>:\u003C/p>\n\u003C!-- snippet: playwright -->\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">public\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> static\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> async\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Task\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> AnEmptyBasketCostsNothing\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">IPage\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> page)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    using\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> IDisposable\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> capture \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> AssurancePlaywright.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Capture\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(page);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    _ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Scenario.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Define\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"An empty basket costs nothing\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Given\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"An empty basket\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> page.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">GotoAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"/basket\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">When\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"The total is worked out\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> page.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">ClickAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"#update-total\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Then\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"It is zero\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">async\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Assert.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Equal\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"£0.00\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> page.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">InnerTextAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"#total\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">)))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">VerifyAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>See \u003Ca href=\"/assurance/docs/adapters/#playwright\">Playwright\u003C/a> for its options.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"migrate-with-an-ai-agent\">Migrate with an AI agent\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>The AHR Assurance skill teaches an AI coding agent to write, convert and review scenarios. Install it from the \u003Ca href=\"https://github.com/AHRConsulting/agent-skills\">AHR Consulting agent skills\u003C/a> catalogue, whose readme gives the steps for each agent. Then ask, for example:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"text\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan>Convert the tests in Billing.Tests to Assurance scenarios, keeping their framework and assertions.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The agent wraps each test's existing code in named steps, so the tests check what they checked before. Review the step names: they are what the report says.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"write-a-scenario\">Write a scenario\u003C/h2>\n\u003C!-- snippet: first-scenario -->\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">[\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Fact\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">public\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Task\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> ASavedDocumentOpensOfflineAsAScenario\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">()\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">    Document\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> expected \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"handbook\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"Offline-ready field handbook\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">    FakeDocumentSource\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> source \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(expected);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">    FakeInMemoryDocumentCache\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> cache \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">    DocumentReader\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> reader \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> FakeOfflineConnectivity\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(), source, cache);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">    DocumentReadResult\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">? result \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-literal)\"> null\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Scenario.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Define\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"A returning offline reader opens a saved handbook\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Given\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"An offline reader with a saved document\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> cache.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Seed\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(expected))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">When\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"The reader opens the handbook\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">async\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> token \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> result \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> reader.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">OpenAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"handbook\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, token))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Then\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"The saved document is returned\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Assert.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Equal\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(expected, result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">.Document))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">And\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"The web source is not contacted\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Assert.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Equal\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-number)\">0\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, source.DownloadCalls))\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        .\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">VerifyAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>Define\u003C/code> names the guarantee. \u003Ccode>Given\u003C/code> sets up, \u003Ccode>When\u003C/code> acts, and \u003Ccode>Then\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>And\u003C/code> check.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Steps use ordinary assertions. A failed check makes the scenario unsatisfied, and the test fails as it would without Assurance.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>VerifyAsync\u003C/code> runs the steps, records the evidence and passes or fails the test.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>result\u003C/code> holds what the \u003Ccode>When\u003C/code> returned. A \u003Ccode>When\u003C/code> can also \u003Ca href=\"/assurance/docs/scenarios/#checking-what-a-when-returned\">return it to the checks\u003C/a> after it.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"run-it-and-report-it\">Run it and report it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">dotnet\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> test\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">dotnet\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> assurance\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\"> report\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>dotnet test\u003C/code> runs the scenarios as before, and the test output shows each one's steps and verdicts. \u003Ccode>dotnet assurance report\u003C/code> then builds the report: for the project in a test project's folder, or for every test project in one report in a solution's folder.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cimg src=\"/assurance/assets/solution-report-example.png\" alt=\"A solution report with one row for each test project\">\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>The report is written for people outside the team. For failure details, expected and actual values and test names, add \u003Ccode>--developer\u003C/code>. To build it in a pipeline, see \u003Ca href=\"/assurance/docs/ci/\">Running in CI\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n",[6,10,13,16],{"id":7,"text":8,"level":9},"install","Install",2,{"id":11,"text":12,"level":9},"migrate-with-an-ai-agent","Migrate with an AI agent",{"id":14,"text":15,"level":9},"write-a-scenario","Write a scenario",{"id":17,"text":18,"level":9},"run-it-and-report-it","Run it and report it","docs/getting-started.md"],"uses":{"params":["page","product"]}}]}
